From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: katamaran <katamaran@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:50:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] tap: read vfkit frames straight into gVisor buffers

Reading each frame into a scratch slice and copying it into a new
buffer kept the reading goroutine busy on a fast upload. Read a frame
into a pooled 64 KiB gVisor view and pass that view to the stack; small
frames are still copied out, so an ACK does not take (and zero) a fresh
64 KiB chunk. recvmsg reports truncated datagrams, which are dropped.
